  "measurement_limitations": [
    "Full purchase uses gross CALL gas plus ordinary intrinsic gas and calldata floor. Account warmth, outer CALL overhead, and refunds differ from top-level receipts.",
    "The scenarios use existing EOA payout recipients, local token mocks, no external NFT mint case at 64 lines, and no swap route.",
    "The hash table preserves group order and checks full grouping equality. Deliberately colliding hash buckets can still make lookups quadratic.",
    "Microbenchmarks include external ABI encoding and return processing. Use the full purchase comparison for end-to-end savings.",
    "The 64-line experiment raises only the temporary MAX_ORDER_LINES to 128. Production limits and files remain unchanged.",
    "The original inherited Cart test methods were removed only in the temporary fixture. The capacity builder uses an external self-call to avoid optimizer duplication. Both variants use the same builder and fixture.",
    "The hash-buffer variant was checked by differential fuzzing and malformed payload tests. It was not combined with the payout variant in full purchase measurements.",
    "Unconditional hash-table grouping regresses the one-group and two-group workloads measured separately. Its full purchase gains apply to dispersed payout groups. An adaptive small-group path requires investigation before adopting it for typical carts."
  ],
